  "title": "Method of Ziyarah of Holy Prophet (s) in Madinah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The method of visiting the shrine of the Holy Prophet (s) is as follows:\n\nWhen you arrive in the holy city of al-Madinah, you may bathe yourself, preparing yourself for the ziyarah. When you intend to enter The Holy Prophet’s Mosque, you should stop at the door of the mosque and say the FIRST form of asking permission for entering there (which has been mentioned in the previous chapter). You may enter from the Gate of Archangel Gabriel (Bab Jibra’il) preceding the right foot to the left. You may then repeat the following phrase one hundred times:\nاَللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nAALLHU AAKBARU\nThe method of visiting the shrine of the Holy Prophet (s) is as follows:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا نَبِيَّ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ بَلَّغْتَ الرِّسَالَةَ وَ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ وَ اٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ وَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَ نَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَ عَبَدْتَ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا حَتّٰىۤ اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ فَصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكَ وَ رَحْمَتُهٗ وَ عَلٰۤى اَهْلِ بَيْتِكَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ.\nAALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA RASUWLA I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA NABIYA I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA MUHAMADA BNA A'ABDI I AALSALAAMU A'ALAYKA YAA KHAATAMA ALNABIYIYNA AASHHADU AANAKA QAD BALAGHTA ALRISAALAHA WA AAQAMTA ALSALAAHA WA AAATAYTA ALZAKAAHA WA AAMARTA BIALMAA'RUWFI WA NAHAYTA A'ANI ALMUNKARI WA A'ABADTA A MUKHLISANA HATAAAA AATAAKA ALYAQIYNU FASALAWAATU I A'ALAYKA WA RAHMATUHU WA A'ALAAAA AAHLI BAYTIKA ALTAAHIRIYNA.\nWhen you arrive in the holy city of al-Madinah, you may bathe yourself, preparing yourself for the ziyarah. When you intend to enter The Holy Prophet’s Mosque, you should stop at the door of the mosque and say the FIRST form of asking permission for entering there (which has been mentioned in the previous chapter). You may enter from the Gate of Archangel Gabriel (Bab Jibra’il) preceding the right foot to the left. You may then repeat the following phrase one hundred times:\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ وَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَ اَنَّكَ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ وَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ بَلَّغْتَ رِسَالَاتِ رَبِّكَ وَ نَصَحْتَ لِاُمَّتِكَ وَ جَاهَدْتَ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَ عَبَدْتَ اللّٰهَ حَتّٰىۤ اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَ الْمَوْعِظَةِ الْحَسَنَةِ وَ اَدَّيْتَ الَّذِيْ عَلَيْكَ مِنَ الْحَقِّ وَ اَنَّكَ قَدْ رَؤُفْتَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ غَلُظْتَ عَلَى الْكَافِرِيْنَ فَبَلَغَ اللّٰهُ بِكَ اَفْضَلَ شَرَفِ مَحَلِّ الْمُكَرَّمِيْنَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اسْتَنْقَذَنَا بِكَ مِنَ الشِّرْكِ وَ الضَّلَالَةِ. اَللّٰهُمَّ فَاجْعَلْ صَلَوَاتِكَ وَ صَلَوَاتِ مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ وَ اَنْبِيَاۤئِكَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ وَ عِبَادِكَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ وَ اَهْلِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَ الْاَرَضِيْنَ وَ مَنْ سَبَّحَ لَكَ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ مِنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ عَبْدِكَ وَ رَسُوْلِكَ وَ نَبِيِّكَ وَ اَمِيْنِكَ وَ نَجِيْبِكَ وَ حَبِيْبِكَ وَ صَفِيِّكَ وَ خَآصَّتِكَ وَ صَفْوَتِكَ وَ خِيَرَتِكَ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ اَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِهِ الدَّرَجَةَ الرَّفِيْعَةَ وَ اٰتِهِ الْوَسِيْلَةَ مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ وَ ابْعَثْهُ مَقَامًا مَحْمُوْدًا يَغْبِطُهٗ بِهِ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرُوْنَ اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ قُلْتَ وَ لَوْ اَنَّهُمْ اِذْ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ جَاۤءُوْكَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوْا اللّٰهَ وَ اسْتَغْفَرَ لَهٗمُ الرَّسُوْلُ لَوَجَدُوْا اللّٰهَ تَوَّابًا رَحِيْمًا وَ اِنِّيْۤ اَتَيْتُكَ مُسْتَغْفِرًا تَاۤئِبًا مِنْ ذُنُوْبِيً وَ اِنِّيْۤ اَتَوَجَّهُ بِكَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رَبِّيْ وَ رَبِّكَ لِيَغْفِرَ لِيْ ذُنُوْبِيْ.\nAASHHADU AAN LAA AILAAHA AILAA U WAHDAHU LAA SHARIYKA LAHU WA AASHHADU AANA MUHAMADANA A'ABDUHU WA RASUWLUHU WA AASHHADU AANAKA RASUWLU I WA AANAKA MUHAMADU BNU A'ABDI I WA AASHHADU AANAKA QAD BALAGHTA RISAALAATI RABIKA WA NASAHTA LIAUMATIKA WA JAAHADTA FIY SABIYLI I WA A'ABADTA A HATAAAA AATAAKA ALYAQIYNU BIALHIKMAHI WA ALMAWA'IZAHI ALHASANAHI WA AADAYTA ALADHIY A'ALAYKA MINA ALHAQI WA AANAKA QAD RA'UFTA BIALMU'MINIYNA WA GHALUZTA A'ALAAA ALKAAFIRIYNA FABALAGHA U BIKA AAFDALA SHARAFI MAHALI ALMUKARAMIYNA ALHAMDU LILAAHI ALADHIY ASTANQADHANAA BIKA MINA ALSHIRKI WA ALDALAALAHI. AALLAAHUMA FAAJA'AL SALAWAATIKA WA SALAWAATI MALAA'IKATIKA ALMUQARABIYNA WA AANBIYAA'IKA ALMURSALIYNA WA A'IBAADIKA ALSAALIHIYNA WA AAHLI ALSAMAAWAATI WA ALAARADIYNA WA MAN SABAHA LAKA YAA RABA ALA'AALAMIYNA MINA ALAAWALIYNA WA ALAAAKHIRIYNA A'ALAAAA MUHAMADIN A'ABDIKA WA RASUWLIKA WA NABIYIKA WA AAMIYNIKA WA NAJIYBIKA WA HABIYBIKA WA SAFIYIKA WA KHAAAASATIKA WA SAFWATIKA WA KHIYARATIKA MIN KHALQIKA AALLAAHUMA AAA'TIHI ALDARAJAHA ALRAFIYA'AHA WA AAATIHI ALWASIYLAHA MINA ALJANAHI WA ABA'ATHHU MAQAAMANA MAHMUWDANA YAGHBITUHU BIHI ALAAWALUWNA WA ALAAAKHIRUWNA AALLAAHUMA AINAKA QULTA WA LAW AANAHUM AIDH ZALAMUWA AANFUSAHUM JAA'UWKA FAASTAGHFARUWA A WA ASTAGHFARA LAHUMU ALRASUWLU LAWAJADUWA A TAWAABANA RAHIYMANA WA AINIY AATAYTUKA MUSTAGHFIRANA TAA'IBANA MIN DHUNUWBIYAN WA AINIY AATAWAJAHU BIKA AILAAA I RABIY WA RABIKA LIYAGHFIRA LIY DHUNUWBIY.\nAllah is the Most Great\nاَسْاَلُ اللّٰهَ الَّذِيْ اجْتَبَاكَ وَ اخْتَارَكَ وَ هَدَاكَ وَ هَدٰى بِكَ اَنْ يُصَلِّيَ عَلَيْكَ.\nAASAALU A ALADHIY AJTABAAKA WA AKHTAARAKA WA HADAAKA WA HADAAAA BIKA AAN YUSALIYA A'ALAYKA.\nYou may then offer the two unit prayer of Greeting the Mosque (tahiyyat al-masjid). After that, you may walk to the holy chamber that includes the tomb of the Holy Prophet. There, you may touch it with your hand, kiss it, and say the following:\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ وَ مَلَاۤئِكَتَهٗ يُصَلُّوْنَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ يَاۤ اَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا صَلُّوْا عَلَيْهِ وَ سَلِّمُوْا تَسْلِيْمًا.\nAINA A WA MALAA'IKATAHU YUSALUWNA A'ALAAA ALNABIYI YAA AAYUHAA ALADHIYNA AAAMANUWA SALUWA A'ALAYHI WA SALIMUWA TASLIYMANA.\nPeace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet of Allah. Peace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of 'Abdullah. Peace be upon you, O Seal of the Prophets. I bear witness that you conveyed the Mission, performed the prayers, gave alms, enjoined the right, forbade the wrong, and served Almighty Allah sincerely until death came upon you Blessings and mercy of Allah be upon you and upon your Household, the Immaculate."
